B.axA=new A.c(B.aOj,["Use the business\u2019s name or a private reference. This is a label, not a calculated amount.","Use the seller\u2019s quoted business price. Keep property priced separately unless it is explicitly included.","Add sales for a consistent 12-month period, before subtracting operating expenses.","Start with net income and add back interest, income taxes, depreciation and amortization. Reconcile it with the statements.","Total the individual nonrecurring or owner-specific costs you can document. Exclude ongoing costs needed by the buyer.","Total owner salary and benefits already deducted in reported EBITDA. Enter 0 when they are already excluded.","Estimate the annual salary and benefits required to replace the owner\u2019s actual duties.","Estimate annual spending needed to keep existing operating assets usable; separate expansion projects.","Use the lower supported enterprise-value-to-EBITDA multiple from comparable transactions.","Use the upper supported comparable multiple. Keep it at or above the low multiple.","Cash paid toward the price \xf7 asking price \xd7 100. Enter 25 for 25%, not 0.25.","Use the annual loan interest rate as a percentage. Enter 7 for 7%.","Use the loan\u2019s amortization period in years, which can differ from its renewal term.","Use the quoted price for the assets included in this transaction.","Add supported current market values for the included equipment and vehicles, rather than their original purchase costs.","Count usable included stock and apply its supportable sale value. Exclude obsolete or unsaleable items.","Add transferable customer balances expected to be collected, after allowances for doubtful accounts.","Use supportable values for transferable rights. Confirm that licenses and contracts can actually be assigned.","Total cash that the agreement says will transfer at closing. Exclude cash retained by the seller.","Total the debts and obligations the buyer will assume under the agreement.","Total supported repair or replacement costs for deferred upkeep of the included assets.","Add estimated legal, appraisal, transfer and other purchase costs without counting them twice.","Recoverable noncash asset proceeds \xf7 their stated noncash asset value \xd7 100. Enter 60 for 60%.","Use the property\u2019s name or your private reference. It identifies the scenario.","Use the quoted property purchase price; keep separately priced business assets out of this amount.","Add annual scheduled rent for all rentable units at the assumed occupancy before vacancy loss.","Add annual recurring parking, storage and other property income outside base rent.","Estimated annual vacancy and credit loss \xf7 potential gross income \xd7 100. Enter 5 for 5%.","Add recurring annual property operating costs. Exclude loan payments, income tax and reserves entered separately.","Estimate annual funding for major component replacement over time. Avoid counting the same cost in operating expenses.","Comparable stabilized NOI \xf7 property value \xd7 100. The calculator estimates value as stabilized NOI \xf7 the cap rate in decimal form.","Cash down payment \xf7 property asking price \xd7 100. Enter 30 for 30%.","Use the property loan\u2019s annual interest rate as a percentage; enter 6.5 for 6.5%.","Use the property loan\u2019s amortization period in years, rather than its renewal term.","Enter the number of years between purchase and the assumed sale.","Use the expected annual change in NOI as a percentage. The scenario compounds it over the hold period.","Use a supported cap rate for the assumed sale. Projected exit NOI divided by this rate gives the scenario\u2019s sale value.","Start with net income and add interest, income taxes, depreciation and amortization. Reconcile it with your annual statements.","Add documented nonrecurring costs that will not continue for a new owner. Enter 0 when there are none.","Total your salary and benefits already deducted in EBITDA. Enter 0 if EBITDA already excludes them.","Estimate the annual salary and benefits required to replace your operating duties.","Use the lower supported EBITDA multiple from comparable business sales.","Use the upper supported comparable multiple, at or above the lower multiple.","Add supportable market values of physical assets included in the sale.","Count usable included inventory and apply supportable sale values, excluding obsolete stock.","Total transferable customer balances likely to be collected, after doubtful-account allowances.","Total obligations the buyer will assume. Keep debt you repay at closing out of this amount.","Use your proposed or agreed gross sale price before fees, debt repayment and payment deferrals.","Total the part of the price payable after closing. It cannot exceed the sale price; enter 0 if none.","Add broker, legal, valuation and other selling costs. Enter 0 where no costs apply.","Total business debt discharged from sale proceeds at closing. Do not include liabilities assumed by the buyer."],t.w)
